---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Favour Nwabude, Android consultant"
  description="Android consultant in Nigeria, working remotely. I focus on how Android apps protect keys, sessions and data on a device they do not control."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="section-label">About</p>
    <h1>Favour Nwabude</h1>
    <p class="treatises-lede">
      An Android consultant in Nigeria, working remotely. My focus is how an Android app protects
      keys, sessions and data on a device it does not control.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>I build and test on a phone, and it makes me read the toolchain</h2>
    <p>
      I work inside a Linux container on my phone (Termux and Ubuntu) with Neovim, Git and Gradle. No
      laptop, no IDE. It forces me to understand the toolchain instead of trusting it. For a client,
      that means I read the code and the platform source, reproduce behaviour on a real device, and
      write down what I verified and what I could not.
    </p>

    <h2>Three years of production Android, learned from security-focused code</h2>
    <p>
      Over three years I have built production Android applications entirely on-device, studying
      security-focused codebases from the ground up and applying those patterns to real work.
      Cleanthes is my main project.
    </p>

    <h2>I publish what I can verify</h2>
    <p>
      I write treatises on Android internals, Linux and the JVM. Each one names the version I checked
      against and how to reproduce it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <footer class="treatise-end">
    <div class="treatise-cta">
      <a class="work-link" href="/#contact">Start a conversation</a>
    </div>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
